# Wattle the Phrase-Keeper — first meeting (Cradle Root)
Wattle: * Tch. A phrase for a phrase. Sit down, dreamer.
Wattle: * The flower in the stone gap told me a word once. I keep it. I keep all of them.
Wattle: * It said: "yours." Just that. Then it closed.
Wattle: * (The bird says it back, wrong somehow, like a coat worn inside out.)
